WEBVTT

00:03.753 --> 00:05.672
Argh!

00:05.755 --> 00:08.174
Damn it, you guys too?!

00:08.258 --> 00:11.302
Julie's got family stuff,
and Ken's in mourning?!

00:11.386 --> 00:13.346
Why it has to be <i>now</i>?

00:13.596 --> 00:14.723
What now?

00:14.806 --> 00:17.017
At this rate, I won't have enough members.

00:18.852 --> 00:22.397
(Automatic Translation)

00:22.480 --> 00:26.401
As things are, I will lose
without even fighting.

00:26.901 --> 00:30.196
I gotta do something to
get two more members.

00:30.697 --> 00:33.116
That said, it can't just be anybody.

00:33.992 --> 00:37.537
I need skilled players who can
compete against strong foes.

00:40.582 --> 00:42.250
It's no use.

00:42.333 --> 00:46.087
I'm scared to even think how much
I will owe them after this.

00:46.838 --> 00:50.258
But <i>they</i> are the only help I can think of.

00:50.341 --> 00:54.262
(Sunraku) (Pencil Knight)

00:54.345 --> 00:59.601
I gotta invite those two to
the Global Game Competition.

01:00.185 --> 01:03.772
Or else I can't beat <i>her</i>.

01:03.855 --> 01:05.982
(Send)

01:15.742 --> 01:17.077
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:20.997 --> 01:22.624
<i>We are the frontiers</i>

01:26.044 --> 01:27.796
<i>Confront with no fear</i>

01:27.879 --> 01:29.964
<i>From zero to a hundred in an instant</i>

01:30.048 --> 01:32.634
<i>Unveiling mysteries hidden</i>
<i>deep in the dark</i>

01:33.218 --> 01:35.178
<i>Even dead, I rise from the dust</i>

01:35.261 --> 01:37.722
<i>Reaching an unprecedented realm</i>

01:37.806 --> 01:40.016
<i>Trying your uniqueness</i>

01:40.099 --> 01:41.267
<i>It's a test level EX</i>

01:41.351 --> 01:42.644
<i>I'm the best, nothing less</i>

01:42.727 --> 01:45.188
<i>Pioneering from the east to the west</i>

01:45.271 --> 01:47.941
<i>Erasing all who resist, their data and all</i>

01:48.024 --> 01:49.192
<i>Did I really win?</i>

01:49.275 --> 01:50.485
<i>What are these tears?</i>

01:50.568 --> 01:52.904
<i>Who will be hated or loved</i>
<i>by the god of victory?</i>

01:52.987 --> 01:54.197
<i>To Each, their own wishes</i>

01:54.280 --> 01:55.281
<i>With friends, aiming for prize</i>

01:55.365 --> 01:57.325
<i>Seeking answers,</i>
<i>cutting through the unknown</i>

01:57.408 --> 01:58.701
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:58.785 --> 02:01.162
<i>Bugged out world, I'm a survivor</i>

02:01.246 --> 02:03.581
<i>Blazing with the guiding fire</i>

02:03.665 --> 02:05.458
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

02:05.542 --> 02:06.626
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

02:06.709 --> 02:08.044
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

02:08.128 --> 02:08.711
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

02:08.795 --> 02:11.673
<i>Declare war. At the system, we aim back</i>

02:11.756 --> 02:14.134
<i>Lose yourself, and it's game over</i>

02:14.217 --> 02:16.052
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

02:16.136 --> 02:16.886
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

02:16.970 --> 02:18.263
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

02:18.346 --> 02:19.681
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

02:23.685 --> 02:25.103
<i>We are the frontiers</i>

02:28.815 --> 02:30.316
<i>Confront with no fear</i>

02:31.234 --> 02:32.443
<i>You know I'll be there</i>

02:32.527 --> 02:33.695
<i>Overturning limits</i>

02:33.778 --> 02:35.488
<i>Now is the new beginning</i>

02:40.243 --> 02:43.705
Well then, that was a pretty
sweet surprise finding,

02:43.788 --> 02:45.915
but it's time to visit Rabituza.

02:45.999 --> 02:47.917
I will open the gate.

02:52.338 --> 02:55.425
Thank you for all the help today, Rei.

02:55.508 --> 02:58.761
O-Oh, no. I had some fun myself, too.

02:58.845 --> 03:03.766
U-Um, if there's anything else I can
help you with, please just tell me.

03:04.183 --> 03:06.185
I'll let you know, then.

03:06.269 --> 03:07.854
Please do!

03:08.771 --> 03:14.402
<i>Aah, if only I could go to Rabituza,</i>
<i>then I could spend more time with him.</i>

03:14.485 --> 03:17.947
<i>But this is a great leap forward for me!</i>

03:18.031 --> 03:20.867
<i>I mustn't let myself get too greedy.</i>

03:20.950 --> 03:24.996
<i>Oh, right. What am I gonna</i>
<i>tell my sister about this?</i>

03:25.079 --> 03:27.790
<i>If I told her the truth…</i>

03:27.874 --> 03:31.502
Sunraku-san and I beat Lycagon.

03:31.586 --> 03:33.379
But it was her shadow, a fake.

03:33.463 --> 03:34.714
What?!

03:34.797 --> 03:38.384
You gotta do it again, then!
And bring me along this time!

03:38.468 --> 03:42.013
C'mon guys! We gotta find
Sunraku-kun and capture him!

03:42.096 --> 03:43.848
We gotta get his cooperation!

03:43.932 --> 03:44.974
Got it, boss!

03:45.058 --> 03:49.520
<i>I'd be troubling Hizutome-kun for sure!</i>

03:50.104 --> 03:53.441
Maybe I should keep this from her
for about a week or so.

03:54.192 --> 03:57.362
Are you okay? Those mood swings…

03:57.904 --> 04:00.281
How about you, Akitsuakane?

04:00.365 --> 04:05.870
I'm thinking about checking the town
first before going to Rabituza.

04:05.954 --> 04:06.913
I see.

04:06.996 --> 04:08.790
We'll split up here, then.

04:09.123 --> 04:10.750
See you too, Ceecrue.

04:10.833 --> 04:15.088
Box does not speak.

04:15.171 --> 04:16.589
<i>Rabituza!</i>

04:16.673 --> 04:18.341
<i>Th-That's right!</i>

04:18.424 --> 04:23.096
<i>Unlike me, Akitsuakane-san</i>
<i>can go to and from Rabituza!</i>

04:23.972 --> 04:25.765
Goodbye!

04:25.848 --> 04:26.766
See ya!

04:26.849 --> 04:28.726
Yes! See you later!

04:28.810 --> 04:30.186
<i>This is bad.</i>

04:30.687 --> 04:34.107
<i>At this rate, I'll be left in the dust!</i>

04:35.233 --> 04:38.861
Okay, Psyger-0-san.
We'll be taking our leave.

04:39.112 --> 04:40.613
U-Um!

04:42.156 --> 04:47.996
Th-There's something
I'd like to ask you about.

05:06.931 --> 05:11.185
He's inviting me to the
Global Game Competition, huh?

05:11.269 --> 05:14.063
<i>I'll cover your travel, entry fee, etc.,</i>

05:14.147 --> 05:18.401
<i>so would you both join me at</i>
<i>the Global Game Competition?</i>

05:18.484 --> 05:23.031
<i>All the members who were supposed to join</i>
<i>me had other business, so they couldn't go.</i>

05:23.114 --> 05:27.035
<i>I need to fill two more slots,</i>
<i>or I won't be able to participate.</i>

05:28.036 --> 05:34.459
<i>An enormous event that introduces</i>
<i>numerous games from all over the world, huh.</i>

05:34.542 --> 05:38.796
Even though an important match
against someone he wants to beat,

05:38.880 --> 05:43.760
but all his party members bowed out,
so he might have to forfeit, huh.

05:48.222 --> 05:49.599
What do you think?

05:52.518 --> 05:54.604
"We can make him owe us with this"?

06:00.777 --> 06:06.449
He must be at his wit's end
to rely on the two of us.

06:07.200 --> 06:13.581
This means I'll be meeting Kei Uomi and
Pencilgon; Towa Amane, in real life, huh.

06:14.582 --> 06:16.959
Well, I don't mind participating.

06:17.293 --> 06:21.672
But just when I'm being
pretty busy over here.

06:24.717 --> 06:30.640
165, 166, 167, 168, 169, 170!

06:30.723 --> 06:34.769
Hold on! You gotta rethink this,
Blue Bird-man! Don't be rash!

06:34.852 --> 06:36.813
C-Calm down, Bee-neechan!

06:36.896 --> 06:37.939
Don't get too close! It's dangerous!

06:38.022 --> 06:39.607
Bird-man!

06:39.690 --> 06:43.945
Sorry, Beelach. This has to be done.

06:44.028 --> 06:46.739
178, 179!

06:47.240 --> 06:50.118
And now, it's 180 seconds!

06:53.746 --> 06:56.541
It really shattered into smithereens.

06:56.624 --> 06:58.126
I see.

06:58.209 --> 07:01.963
Just like the one before, this one
flies off after exactly three minutes.

07:02.046 --> 07:06.843
Regardless of defense stat, seems like
Contusion breaks everything all the same.

07:06.926 --> 07:11.389
Ya dang fool! How mucha my stuff
ya goin' to break till yer satisfied, eh?!

07:11.889 --> 07:15.184
Studying now Lycagon's Contusion
works is important, okay.

07:15.268 --> 07:18.563
If I don't fully grasp how it works,
I may get into trouble later.

07:18.646 --> 07:23.317
Like I said! Don't test it…
with the armor I made!

07:23.401 --> 07:28.448
I wanna know if high-def armor
breaks at the exact same time, okay.

07:28.531 --> 07:30.908
But now I get the gist of it.

07:31.576 --> 07:36.122
Regardless of the armor's quality,
it will break off after three minutes.

07:36.581 --> 07:39.667
I bet the same goes for
Non-Standard Tactical Gear.

07:39.750 --> 07:45.923
In that case, I better think of it as more
of a temporary "buff" than an armor.

07:46.507 --> 07:50.720
It is quite a pain having to pay
attention to the three-minute limit,

07:50.803 --> 07:53.848
but it does give me
more options in battle.

07:53.931 --> 07:56.350
It doesn't sound all that bad
thinking it that way.

07:56.434 --> 07:58.060
Good grief.

07:58.144 --> 08:00.938
You're wreckin' way
too mucha my stuff.

08:01.939 --> 08:07.028
Ooh! You already finished the Gilta
Brille repair I asked before I sleep?

08:07.111 --> 08:09.489
Now that's the Ancient
Craftsman Beelach for you!

08:09.572 --> 08:11.699
Treat it with more care will ya?

08:11.782 --> 08:15.453
It ain't easy to fix a Re-Legacy Weapon,
ya know?

08:15.536 --> 08:20.124
Well, since I'm here, can you enhance
some weapons and fix some gears for me?

08:20.208 --> 08:22.293
Say what?! There's still more?!

08:22.376 --> 08:25.630
Relax! I got the mahni to spare.

08:25.713 --> 08:30.259
Peatz bought a bunch of materials
from us, so we got plenty!

08:30.343 --> 08:33.930
I don't have much time before
my meet-up with Rust and Mordo!

08:34.013 --> 08:35.890
Rush it for me, okay?

08:35.973 --> 08:38.476
Beelach! I know you can do it!

08:38.559 --> 08:39.519
You can do it!

08:39.602 --> 08:42.021
You can do it! You can do it!
You can do it! You can do it!

08:42.104 --> 08:45.775
How much work are
ya gonna make me, huh?!

08:47.610 --> 08:53.533
(Fifticia Shipyard)

08:53.616 --> 08:58.496
Man, I had no idea fixing and
enhancing stuff would cost this much.

08:59.121 --> 09:01.874
It blew away practically
everything I earned.

09:02.792 --> 09:04.919
She seemed pissed off, too.

09:05.002 --> 09:07.380
She didn't rip me off, did she?

09:07.463 --> 09:11.300
She's not like Eevell-oneechan.
She'd never do that.

09:11.384 --> 09:13.469
Hey, no talking.

09:13.553 --> 09:15.888
Stay in your disguise.

09:15.972 --> 09:19.892
Mmmh! I'd rather walk in my human form.

09:19.976 --> 09:23.896
We gotta conserve on mana potions.
Endure it, okay?

09:24.647 --> 09:25.898
Still…

09:26.774 --> 09:31.070
There sure are a lot of
rowdy-looking NPCs here.

09:31.153 --> 09:36.492
Quite a place you pick
for a meet-up, guys.

09:37.785 --> 09:39.161
Is it that shop?

09:48.754 --> 09:50.965
Damn, you've really done it!

09:51.048 --> 09:52.425
I'll make you pay!

09:52.842 --> 09:54.343
You okay, man?

09:54.427 --> 09:55.344
Huh?

09:55.428 --> 09:58.222
Shut up! Don't talk to me???

10:00.141 --> 10:01.767
You…

10:02.893 --> 10:05.563
N-No, nevermind.

10:06.689 --> 10:08.733
Hey, calm down!

10:08.816 --> 10:11.068
Shut up, Mordo! This should be the way!

10:11.652 --> 10:14.905
Mordo… and Rust, maybe?

10:14.989 --> 10:18.159
- Should I hit them harder?
- You're going too far!

10:18.242 --> 10:19.702
Cut it out, Rust!

10:20.494 --> 10:24.665
<i>They must be Rust and Mordo here in</i> SLF<i>.</i>

10:24.749 --> 10:27.335
Whoa, what are you guys doing?

10:27.418 --> 10:31.339
For someone so tiny, you've sure
got the worst temper here.

10:32.256 --> 10:34.091
- What did you say?
- Are you…

10:34.175 --> 10:35.259
You…

10:36.010 --> 10:37.428
Rust! Wait!

10:37.511 --> 10:40.181
Shut up, you half-naked freak!

10:40.264 --> 10:41.515
Huh?

10:49.065 --> 10:51.484
- I can't see! What happened, Mordo?!
- Waaa! What's this?! What's this?!

10:51.567 --> 10:55.529
Hold it, hold it! That guy is not an NPC!

10:55.613 --> 10:56.530
What?

10:56.864 --> 11:01.285
Even if I was, don't just punch
people out of nowhere.

11:02.203 --> 11:05.581
Your avatar sure feels a lot
different than from over <i>Nephilim</i>.

11:05.665 --> 11:07.541
Rust. Mordo.

11:08.334 --> 11:09.877
Sunraku…

11:10.795 --> 11:12.755
And what's up with you?

11:12.838 --> 11:16.884
Your bird-head and kinky half-naked
getup is nothing short of strange.

11:16.967 --> 11:17.802
Your kink?

11:17.885 --> 11:19.595
Of course not!

11:19.678 --> 11:22.181
<i>I'm sick of this conversation already.</i>

11:24.433 --> 11:25.976
I see.

11:26.060 --> 11:29.605
So after you crashed Lycagon's chin,
she toyed around with you?

11:29.688 --> 11:32.775
Lycagon's a Unique Monster, right?

11:32.858 --> 11:34.110
That's incredible.

11:34.193 --> 11:37.530
I had to go around
half-naked before that, though.

11:37.613 --> 11:40.199
But yeah, we have a long history.

11:42.493 --> 11:45.329
The stares are killing me
because I'm with a freak like you.

11:45.413 --> 11:48.457
You sure it's not because
you beat the crap out of them?

11:49.166 --> 11:52.795
Is that talking Vorpal Bunny
also part of your "Unique"?

11:52.878 --> 11:53.879
Yeah.

11:54.630 --> 11:57.007
I'm Emul! Nice to meet you!

11:57.091 --> 11:58.926
Nice to meet you too.

11:59.009 --> 12:00.886
<i>SLF</i> sure is something.

12:00.970 --> 12:03.055
Including that robot stuff,

12:03.139 --> 12:05.349
there sure are a lot of things
nobody knows yet.

12:05.850 --> 12:08.644
You better not be lying
about that robot thing.

12:08.727 --> 12:11.105
Yeah, same to you.

12:11.856 --> 12:18.154
So, I'd like to take on that Unique Scenario
connected to the Ctarnidd of the Abyss.

12:18.237 --> 12:25.870
Well, we actually came here early
to look for the NPC who'll lead us to it.

12:25.953 --> 12:28.164
But we haven't been able to find him.

12:28.247 --> 12:31.667
Huh? Whoa, are you sure about this?

12:31.750 --> 12:36.422
We actually don't know
exactly what triggers it.

12:36.505 --> 12:42.303
Last time, when I was beating up
all the mean-looking NPCs here,

12:42.386 --> 12:46.015
an NPC who claimed to be the "Messenger
of the Great Pirate" came up to me

12:46.098 --> 12:49.268
and led me to this guy called
the "Great Pirate Stude."

12:49.810 --> 12:52.271
"Great Pirate Stude"?

12:53.189 --> 12:57.651
So that "Stude" guy is the one
who gives the Unique Scenario?

12:57.735 --> 12:59.069
That's right.

12:59.153 --> 13:00.696
That's why Rust…

13:00.779 --> 13:04.783
I figured doing the same thing as
the last time would make him show up.

13:06.619 --> 13:10.498
So that's how you started to punch
everyone in this joint?

13:10.581 --> 13:12.875
She was so violent, she scared me.

13:12.958 --> 13:17.963
Good thing it's still early in the morning,
or else other players could've seen us.

13:18.047 --> 13:21.592
Besides, beating up NPC
is weird in the first place.

13:21.675 --> 13:24.386
They were the ones who started it.

13:25.554 --> 13:31.185
So in short, we must first meet this
"Messenger of the Great Pirate" guy?

13:31.268 --> 13:32.978
He'll be coming here soon, I believe.

13:33.062 --> 13:36.190
You really think so?

13:52.164 --> 13:56.252
Hah! I was wondering what caused
all the racket. So it really was you!

13:56.335 --> 14:01.840
Haven't seen you for a while, I thought
you got scared and ran away, you pipsqueak!

14:05.010 --> 14:06.262
Hey, don't tell me…

14:06.345 --> 14:10.933
This tiny brat isn't the "Messenger
of the Great Pirate" guy, right?

14:11.016 --> 14:12.518
N-No, he's…

14:12.601 --> 14:13.852
Messenger?

14:15.229 --> 14:17.064
What are you talking about?

14:18.023 --> 14:24.071
I am none other than the Great
Pirate Stude himself! In flesh!

14:24.154 --> 14:26.740
(Self-Styled: Great Pirate Stude)

14:29.368 --> 14:30.411
Huh?

14:30.494 --> 14:32.329
Stude?

14:32.413 --> 14:34.665
Then, this guy is…

14:34.748 --> 14:36.375
Yup.

14:36.458 --> 14:42.006
The NPC who gives the Unique Scenario that
likely leads to Ctarnidd of the Abyss…

14:42.756 --> 14:44.758
…is this damn brat.

14:48.596 --> 14:50.806
<i>In Faeria Chronicle Online.</i>

14:51.682 --> 14:53.559
<i>There was once this damn brat named "Ark."</i>

14:53.642 --> 14:55.936
<i>(People call him "Ark Nuisance")</i>

14:56.020 --> 14:59.398
<i>He's an antagonist who took</i>
<i>advantage of his position as</i>

14:59.481 --> 15:02.026
<i>the "Beloved Child of the Spirits" to</i>
<i>hinder the player's progress multiple times.</i>

15:02.943 --> 15:08.574
<i>He framed the protagonist's party,</i>
<i>sends strong foes to kill them,</i>

15:09.158 --> 15:11.535
<i>pour poison into a village's well.</i>

15:11.952 --> 15:14.121
<i>set monsters on loose,</i>

15:15.039 --> 15:17.374
<i>set the forest aflame.</i>

15:18.542 --> 15:22.546
<i>steal important weapons, and so on.</i>

15:23.547 --> 15:27.968
<i>The devs who unconscionably made</i>
<i>a scum by the name "Faeria"</i>

15:28.052 --> 15:32.222
<i>purposely designed this</i>
<i>character to piss off the players.</i>

15:32.306 --> 15:35.559
<i>The stress he caused</i>
<i>was no laughing matter.</i>

15:38.228 --> 15:43.484
<i>But thanks to that, my standard</i>
<i>for a damn brat became pretty high.</i>

15:43.567 --> 15:46.987
This lanky dude's as
wispy as always, ain't he?

15:47.071 --> 15:49.281
Hahaha, I'm more of a bookworm, so…

15:49.365 --> 15:54.078
Huh? Bookworm? Ya still
gotta eat more! Eat some meat!

15:55.412 --> 15:57.122
This brat!

15:57.206 --> 16:01.669
<i>He might be a little too</i>
<i>much for Rust and Mordo,</i>

16:01.752 --> 16:04.254
<i>but this's child's play</i>
<i>in my eyes. Cute, even.</i>

16:05.089 --> 16:08.676
Being "bratty" sure is the one and
only characteristic you have, huh?

16:08.759 --> 16:10.135
That did ya say, pipsqueak?!

16:10.219 --> 16:14.390
Oh, that short temper sure
makes him quite the "bratty kid."

16:14.473 --> 16:17.726
Huh? Did you say something, you bird-ma???

16:18.852 --> 16:20.354
Y-You…

16:20.854 --> 16:22.815
You, what's that?

16:22.898 --> 16:24.149
Huh?

16:24.233 --> 16:29.279
Oh, so the NPCs really were
reacting to my Contusion?

16:29.363 --> 16:31.615
You scared some guys
on our way here, too.

16:32.199 --> 16:35.244
The Vorpal Soul leaking
from your body emits pressure

16:35.327 --> 16:39.790
that slashes anyone who comes near you!

16:39.873 --> 16:42.209
What? Is that how it works?

16:42.292 --> 16:44.586
Am I supposed to be like
a sharp knife or something?

16:44.670 --> 16:49.842
M-M-May I ask y-y-your name?!

16:49.925 --> 16:51.885
It's super effective, eh?

16:52.720 --> 16:54.972
My name's Sunraku.

16:55.055 --> 16:57.891
I'm working with these two for now.

16:58.392 --> 16:59.685
Nice to meet 'cha.

16:59.768 --> 17:01.270
I'm good at…

17:04.523 --> 17:07.776
…crushing Lycagon's jaw.

17:11.405 --> 17:13.699
W-W-Wow, really?

17:13.782 --> 17:16.869
He-hehe! Wh-What a bold man!

17:16.952 --> 17:23.250
I-If you work for me,
y-you'll be amply r… rrrr… r…

17:23.333 --> 17:24.418
- Y-Yes!
- Rewarded?

17:24.501 --> 17:27.337
I'll give you a reward!

17:27.421 --> 17:28.505
Don't make him cry.

17:28.589 --> 17:34.428
Sorry, he reminds me of aother snotty brat,
so I can't help but to pick on him.

17:36.847 --> 17:41.226
W-Well then, I'll take you to my ship,
so follow me.

17:41.310 --> 17:42.478
Ship?

17:42.561 --> 17:45.397
Without one, you can't
reach the ship my daddy…

17:45.481 --> 17:46.565
No.

17:47.024 --> 17:53.489
To reach the ship that killed my father,
the Crying Innsman!

17:53.572 --> 17:55.908
Crying Innsman?

17:58.869 --> 18:00.329
Unique Scenario?

18:10.172 --> 18:13.967
<i>We were told about the</i>
<i>ghost ship, "Crying Innsman."</i>

18:14.593 --> 18:17.054
<i>According to Self-Styled</i>
<i>Great Pirate Stude,</i>

18:17.137 --> 18:21.892
<i>the ghost ship will offer its kidnapped</i>
<i>inhabitants to the "Master of the Abyss."</i>

18:24.353 --> 18:25.854
All right!

18:25.938 --> 18:29.650
Let's go catch that ghost ship

18:29.733 --> 18:33.612
and get ourselves introduced
to that "Master of the Abyss"!

18:37.491 --> 18:40.327
The ghost ship that appears
accompanied by a huge storm;

18:40.410 --> 18:42.538
The "Crying Innsman."

18:43.163 --> 18:48.210
My father ran into it and
boarded it all by himself.

18:48.293 --> 18:52.172
He fought the monsters inside
and got his crew to escape.

18:53.674 --> 18:55.425
In exchange for his own life.

18:56.802 --> 18:59.179
So you want revenge?

18:59.429 --> 19:00.389
That's right.

19:00.472 --> 19:03.809
I'll sink that ghost ship
in my father's place.

19:03.892 --> 19:09.273
And when that deed is done,
I will finally be the captain…

19:15.612 --> 19:18.657
…of the Scarlet Whale, the flagship
of the Redwhale Pirates!

19:21.702 --> 19:24.246
So this is your pirate ship?

19:24.329 --> 19:25.747
Looking nice.

19:28.083 --> 19:30.419
Load up our cargo at once, boys!

19:30.669 --> 19:32.337
Aye-aye, sir!

19:32.421 --> 19:34.298
We set sail in an hour!

19:34.381 --> 19:35.799
Don't forget your weapons!

19:36.091 --> 19:37.718
Aye-aye, sir!

19:37.801 --> 19:40.512
Make sure our ballista's at the ready!

19:40.888 --> 19:42.431
Aye-aye, sir!

19:42.514 --> 19:45.142
C'mon! Hurry it up!

19:45.642 --> 19:47.227
Wow.

19:47.311 --> 19:51.190
That Stude sure acts like
a proper captain.

19:51.273 --> 19:54.651
I've never been on a boat before!

19:54.735 --> 19:56.612
I can't wait!

19:56.695 --> 20:00.073
I always swung you around,
so I suppose you'll be all right.

20:00.157 --> 20:02.284
No need to worry about seasick.

20:03.911 --> 20:09.583
Still, Fifticia's a really fancy city,
but this seayard?

20:09.666 --> 20:12.044
This area seems a little sketchier.

20:12.127 --> 20:16.256
This slums was apparently
made in a rush to house

20:16.340 --> 20:21.136
the crews building the ships
to explore the New Land.

20:21.220 --> 20:22.596
I see.

20:22.679 --> 20:26.058
So now the ships are completed,
this temporary housing area

20:26.141 --> 20:29.436
became a hotbed for the lawless, huh?

20:29.519 --> 20:31.521
Make way, make way, make way!

20:31.855 --> 20:36.485
It's the Redwhale Pirates'
famous "Barrel Delivery"!

20:36.777 --> 20:38.904
Huh?! What?!

20:38.987 --> 20:40.489
- Here goes!
- There!

20:41.323 --> 20:43.450
All this stuff is for you!

20:43.533 --> 20:44.660
For me?!

20:44.743 --> 20:47.496
Delivery complete!

20:47.913 --> 20:49.414
Hey!

20:52.000 --> 20:54.503
What's this? Should I take it?

20:54.586 --> 20:57.047
Did we get this before?

20:57.130 --> 20:59.258
Dunno. I don't remember.

21:00.759 --> 21:04.513
This must be supplies for
the ship trip or something.

21:04.596 --> 21:07.432
Weirdly thoughtful of <i>SLF</i> to provide them.

21:07.516 --> 21:09.810
I wonder what's inside!

21:09.893 --> 21:11.353
Let's see…

21:12.145 --> 21:16.817
What's in there? What's in there?

21:19.778 --> 21:22.531
R-R-R-Rei?! Wh-Why?!

21:30.497 --> 21:32.249
We're finally out!

21:32.332 --> 21:34.960
A tight fit, verily.

21:35.210 --> 21:36.878
Akitsuakane too?!

21:38.547 --> 21:41.717
Ceecrue-oniichan! It's only been hours.

21:43.427 --> 21:46.096
Su-Sunraku-san, it's you.

21:46.179 --> 21:49.016
What are you doing here?

21:49.099 --> 21:50.434
Why, you ask?

21:51.018 --> 21:53.061
I should be asking you that.

21:53.562 --> 21:56.565
Or rather, where are we?

22:00.027 --> 22:03.071
How did you two get delivered here?

22:04.323 --> 22:06.700
What's going on?

22:28.555 --> 22:31.058
I hide in my brain every day

22:31.141 --> 22:33.018
cause I'm running out of patience

22:33.685 --> 22:35.479
lost in distorted thoughts

22:35.562 --> 22:39.357
I can't help but hold my breath

22:39.524 --> 22:41.693
blurred mind, spinning in place

22:41.777 --> 22:43.945
I long to turn away from that scene
to close my eyes.

22:44.029 --> 22:45.238
I don't like what I'm seeing

22:45.322 --> 22:46.031
and it's a curse

22:46.114 --> 22:48.241
it's a thorn in my side

22:49.576 --> 22:51.745
Countless eyes and voices

22:51.828 --> 22:58.543
clapping and laughing,
with a nihilistic air

22:58.627 --> 23:00.712
I'm losing my mind

23:00.796 --> 23:03.256
Inside this scary little world

23:03.340 --> 23:08.136
life is gradually soaking up my dopamine

23:08.220 --> 23:09.596
but I can breathe

23:09.679 --> 23:11.223
I can feel like I matter

23:11.306 --> 23:13.266
in my twisted imagination

23:13.350 --> 23:15.769
cause realitYhurts

23:15.852 --> 23:20.607
I think I'd rather stay here

23:25.654 --> 23:30.492
I think I'd rather stay here
